I ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 41. Sosnowy C, Weiss L, Maylahn C, Pirani S, Katagiri N. Evidence-based decision making in local health departments: facilitators and barriers to practice. Am J Prev Med. doi: 10.1016/j.amepre.2013.08.004. In press. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 42. Bekemeier B, Chen A, Kawakyu N, Yang Y. Limited choices: making decisions regarding local public health resource allocation during a financial crisis. Am J Prev Med. doi: 10.1016/j.amepre.2013.08.009. In press. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 43. Riley WJ, Gearin KJ, Parrotta CD, Briggs J, Gyllstrom ME. Local tax support for public health: the roles of fiscal capacity and fiscal effort. Am J Prev Med. doi: 10.1016/j.amepre.2013.08.012. In press. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 44. Satterfield JM, Spring B, Brownson RC, Mullen EJ, Newhouse RP, Walker BB, et al. Toward a transdisciplinary model of evidence-based practice. Milbank Q. 2009 Jun;87(2):368–90. doi: 10.1111/j.1468-0009.2009.00561.x. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 45. Public Health Accreditation Board . Public Health Accreditation Board Standards: An Overview. Public Health Accreditation Board; Alexandria, VA: 2011. [ Google Scholar ] 46. Brownson RC, Allen P, Duggan K, Stamatakis KA, Erwin PC. Fostering more-effective public health by identifying administrative evidence-based practices: a review of the literature. Am J Prev Med. 2012 Sep;43(3):309–19. doi: 10.1016/j.amepre.2012.06.006. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 47. Marshall A, VanRaemdonck L, Bryant L. Colorado public health practice-based research network: Leadership in the early stages of network development. Leadership Public Health. 2011;9(1):12–6. [ Google Scholar ] 48. Consortium from Altarum Institute, CDC, RWJF, National Coordinating Center for PHSSR A national research agenda for public health services and systems. Am J Prev Med. 2012 May;42(5 Suppl 1):S72–8. doi: 10.10